Dear all,

 

Please find attached the draft judgment in this matter from Mr Justice MacDonald.

 

The judge asks you to please note the front page rubric on the judgment.

 

He also asks:

 

When submitting their corrections, the parties should be mindful of the decision of the Court of Appeal in Re I (Children: Fact Finding: Clarification of Judgment) [2019] EWCA Civ 898, [2019] 2 FLR 887 paras [33] to [41] and Mostyn J in Olga Cazalet v Walid Abu-Zalaf [2022] EWFC 119 at [63].

 

This judgment will be handed down on 18 April 2024 with no attendance required.

 

Many thanks

Kind regards

 

Karen Selby-King

 

Clerk to The Honourable Sir Jonathan Cohen

High Court Judge / Judge in charge of Family Division Appeals

 

Clerk to The Honourable Mr Justice MacDonald

Deputy Head of International Family Justice for England & Wales

Family Presiding Judge for London

 

*Also temporary Clerk to The Honourable Ms Justice Russell*

 

Clerks to HM Judges | HMCTS | Royal Courts of Justice | London | WC2A 2LL 

Phone: 0207 947 7426  Mobile: 07591 992371 

 

gov.uk/hmcts 

 

 

Here is how HMCTS uses personal data about you

 

 

 

 
This e-mail and any attachments is intended only for the attention of the addressee(s). Its unauthorised use, disclosure, storage or copying is not permitted. If you are not the intended recipient, please destroy all copies and inform the sender by return e-mail. Internet e-mail is not a secure medium. Any reply to this message could be intercepted and read by someone else. Please bear that in mind when deciding whether to send material in response to this message by e-mail. This e-mail (whether you are the sender or the recipient) may be monitored, recorded and retained by the Ministry of Justice. Monitoring / blocking software may be used, and e-mail content may be read at any time. You have a responsibility to ensure laws are not broken when composing or forwarding e-mails and their contents. 

